  "name": "Profession Upgrade Kits raise a crafted item one quality tier per kit",
  "contract": "Using a profession Upgrade Kit on an item replaces it with the next tier of its quality chain (base, @Refined@, @Superior@, @Masterwork@) when the kit's recipe and the item's recipe share a skill line and a reagent, and consumes one kit. The Copper Bar Upgrade Kit (88254, Blacksmithing recipe from Copper Bar) raises the Copper Chain Belt (2851, Blacksmithing recipe from Copper Bar) to 1152546, 1152547 and 1152548, in the bags and while equipped. A Light Leather Upgrade Kit (85125, Leatherworking) is refused on the belt, and a Masterwork belt has no further tier; neither refusal consumes the kit. The same Light Leather kit raises a Kodo Hide Bag (5081, Leatherworking recipe from Light Leather) to 1154382 in the backpack and to 1154383 while it is equipped in a bag slot, keeping the bag in that slot; a bag holding items is refused without consuming the kit or its contents.",
